# Command cards

Standalone, one-line commands the reader is meant to copy go through `_includes/cmd-card.html`. Do not drop them in a fenced `bash` block.

```liquid
{% include cmd-card.html
   variant="cache"
   badge="users' view"
   cmd="dig www.example.com"
   desc="What do users currently see? Asks the configured resolver." %}
```

If `cmd` contains double quotes, `{% capture %}` the command first, then pass `cmd=the_capture`.

## Variants

| `variant` | Color | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `cache` | purple | resolver / cached view |
| `truth` | teal | authoritative, `+norecurse`, `+trace` |
| `ops` | gray | everything else (rndc, ansible, apt, galaxy) |

Default is `cache` if omitted. Always set it explicitly.

## Not a card

- Inline `` `dig ...` `` inside a sentence
- Multi-step recipes (venv install, heredocs, clone-then-compose)
- Config / YAML / INI
- Command output
- Cheatsheets (the BIND command reference stays one fence)

Wrong: wrapping `python3 -m venv && pip install` as four cards, or promoting "verifiable with `dig @auth +norecurse`" out of a paragraph.
